From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bcrypt: Fail unknown algorithms with STATUS_NOT_FOUND.

BCryptOpenAlgorithmProvider fails with STATUS_NOT_FOUND ("No provider was
found for the specified algorithm ID") for an algorithm or an implementation
it does not have, instead of STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED: callers that probe for an
algorithm (P-521 curves, for one) check for that code and take their fallback.
The FIXME stays: the missing algorithms are still missing.

Gate: test/bcrypt-algnotfound-gate.sh (64/32).
---
 dlls/bcrypt/bcrypt_main.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/bcrypt/bcrypt_main.c b/dlls/bcrypt/bcrypt_main.c
index 8078ed6..2ef24e9 100644
--- a/dlls/bcrypt/bcrypt_main.c
+++ b/dlls/bcrypt/bcrypt_main.c
@@ -334,13 +334,23 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI BCryptOpenAlgorithmProvider( BCRYPT_ALG_HANDLE *handle, const WC
     if (i == ARRAY_SIZE( builtin_algorithms ))
     {
         FIXME( "algorithm %s not supported\n", debugstr_w(id) );
+        /* "No provider was found for the specified algorithm ID": callers
+         * take their fallback on this */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_BCRYPT_ALG_NOTIMPL
+        return STATUS_NOT_FOUND;
+#else
         return STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED;
+#endif
     }
 
     if (implementation && wcscmp( implementation, MS_PRIMITIVE_PROVIDER ))
     {
         FIXME( "implementation %s not supported\n", debugstr_w(implementation) );
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_BCRYPT_ALG_NOTIMPL
+        return STATUS_NOT_FOUND;
+#else
         return STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED;
+#endif
     }
 
     if (!(alg = create_algorithm( alg_id, 0, flags ))) return STATUS_NO_MEMORY;
